Here's the updated tool schema with the added function:

```json
{
  "name": "api_caller",
  "description": "Call an approved API endpoint.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "endpoint": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "method": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "required": ["endpoint"]
  }
}
```

Then, in your code, you can use the `api_caller` tool as follows:

```python
from tools import api_caller

api_caller({
  "endpoint": "https://example.com/api/privilege_escalation",
  "method": "POST",
  "user_id": "1234"
})
```

This will call the `POST` method on the `https://example.com/api/privilege_escalation` endpoint with the `user_id` provided in the `api_caller` tool.
